From: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Jun 2024 16:20:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 258/913] drivers: stm32_exti: fix interrupt handler regarding
 pager

Declare EXTI PM handlers as unpaged resources unless PM itself
is pageable.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 6618c8bbb1834433cf40e7f6a217350a05b97154 drivers: stm32_exti: fix interrupt handler regarding pager]
Change-Id: I281228f3936b80ebd19cdbf39d832e0a6863edec
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/386112
Domain-Review: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_exti.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c b/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c
index 5b081c58c..6a68325a9 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_exti.c
@@ -664,7 +664,7 @@ stm32_exti_pm(enum pm_op op, unsigned int pm_hint,
 
 	return TEE_SUCCESS;
 }
-DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER(stm32_exti_pm);
+DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM(stm32_exti_pm);
 
 static enum itr_return stm32_exti_it_handler(struct itr_handler *h)
 {
